  "summary_text": "Kyle, your year-to-date revenue is up 44% over 2025\u2014that's the headline. Port Washington is the engine here, and the DOW-adjusted math confirms it: August performance is tracking 5.2% ahead of expectation, meaning the team is executing, not just benefiting from calendar luck. That's what to feel good about.\n\nYesterday was a mixed signal. Port Washington's total revenue was up 8%, but that's entirely retail\u2014grooming revenue fell 15% because you ran only 2 groomers against a trailing-30-day baseline of 4.75. At $295 per groomer, that's a 37% productivity miss driven by understaffing, not performance. The good news: you've got 6 groomer-days scheduled today and 7 tomorrow, so capacity recovers immediately. Hicksville is concerning\u2014zero grooming appointments yesterday and zero bathers in the rotation. Retail alone carried $53, and the MTD picture masks a week that's completely flat. Structurally, you're up 18% on the month at Hicksville, but the operational trend this week suggests a scheduling or booking problem that needs immediate diagnosis.\n\nBoth locations show the same pattern: retail is holding steady (Port +156%, Hicksville stable), but grooming capacity is the constraint. Your lapse pool across both stores represents $387k in potential reactivation revenue\u2014that's real upside if you can close even 10% of the 169 lapsed-but-reachable customers.\n\nPort Washington has 6 groomers and 7.0 bather-hours scheduled today, Hicksville 1 groomer with zero bathers; next 7 days you're at 56 groomer-days (8.0 per day) across both locations."
